/-!
# Transitivity of the concrete Held permutation representation

A rooted spanning tree of the ATLAS degree-2058 action assigns every letter
other than zero a predecessor reached by one generator inverse. The checked
rank strictly decreases along predecessors. Induction therefore constructs
an element of the concrete Held subgroup carrying zero to each letter.

The private tables were obtained by breadth-first search on the exact source
permutations in `Model/Source/HeG1-p2058B0.g1` and `.g2`. Lean's kernel checks
every predecessor inequality against the existing permutation definitions;
the search algorithm and its output are not trusted as proof. The reproducible
converter is `Model/Source/generate_transitivity.py`.

Source: ATLAS representation `HeG1-p2058B0`,
https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/permrep/HeG1-p2058B0 .
This establishes the transitive action used in normalizer realization; it
makes no assertion about the order or full automorphism group of Held.
-/

